2. PHP Class for generating random strings and secure hashing passwords:

```php
<?php
class PasswordHelper {
    private $charsets = [];
    private $hashes = ['sha256', 'sha384', 'sha512'];

    public function __construct(array $charsets) {
        $this->charsets = array_merge($this->charsets, $charsets);
    }

    public function generateRandomString($length) {
        if (!is_numeric($length)) {
            throw new Exception("Invalid input: string length must be a number");
        }

        $randomString = '';
        $possibleChars = $this->charsets[array_rand(range(0, count($this->charsets) - 1))];
        while (strlen($randomString) < $length) {
            $randomString .= $possibleChars[array_rand(range(0, strlen($possibleChars) - 1))];
        }

        return $randomString;
    }

    public function hashPassword($password, $algorithm = null) {
        if (!is_string($password)) {
            throw new Exception("Invalid input: password must be a string");
        }

        if (empty($algorithm)) {
            $algorithm = $this->hashes[array_rand(range(0, count($this->hashes) - 1))];
        }

        return hash($algorithm, $password);
    }
}
```

