**In-memory store fallback:**

Use the SessionHandler class in PHP to create a custom session handler:

```php
session_set_save_handler(new class implements SessionHandlerInterface {
    private $storage = [];
    private $gcMaxLifeTime = 60 * 60; // Set session duration in minutes (e.g., 1 hour)

    public function open($savePath, $sessionName): bool {
        return true;
    }

    public function close(): void {
        // Implement eviction policy based on time or number of sessions here
    }

    public function destroy($sessionId): bool {
        unset($_SESSION[$sessionId]);
        unset($this->storage[$sessionId]);
        file_put_contents('session-audit.log', 'Session #' . $sessionId . ' has been invalidated.' . PHP_EOL, FILE_APPEND);
        return true;
    }

    public function read($sessionId): string|false {
        if (!isset($_SESSION[$sessionId])) {
            return false;
        }
        $data = $_SESSION[$sessionId];
        unset($_SESSION[$sessionId]);
        $this->storage[$sessionId] = $data;
        return $data;
    }

    public function write($sessionId, $data): bool {
        if (!is_string($data)) {
            throw new InvalidArgumentException('Session data must be a string.');
        }
        $_SESSION[$sessionId] = json_decode($data);
        $this->storage[$sessionId] = $data;
        return true;
    }
}, true, false);
