The method handles concurrent invocations effectively using a ReentrantLock. It also accounts for temporary failures by gracefully handling delays in the external logging service responses without impacting overall throughput. Developers can specify the type of hash algorithm to use (SHA-256 or SHA-512) and can configure the log level using the `logging.level` system property.

Edge cases and error conditions, such as an unsupported hash algorithm or invalid input, are handled accordingly, ensuring robustness and reliability. The method optimizes performance for high-throughput environments by minimizing latency and resource consumption.']

